# Using SEO data

## Blade (preferred)

`@seo(...)` → `new SEOData(...)` + `SEOService::setData()`. `@seoData` → `render()`.

```blade
<head>
    @seo(
        title: $page->title,
        description: $page->excerpt,
        image: $page->socialImagePath,
        type: 'article',
        publishedAt: $page->published_at,
        modifiedAt: $page->updated_at,
        section: $page->category?->name,
        tags: $page->tagNames,
        canonicalUrl: $page->canonicalUrl,
        lang: $page->hreflangMap,
        schema: [$page->schemaOrgObject],
    )
    @seoData
</head>
```

- Always pair `@seo` with `@seoData` in the same head.
- `@seo` args go **inside** `new SEOData(...)` — named ctor args only. `@seo($data)` is wrong; use `SEOService::setData($data)` in PHP.
- Do not duplicate `<title>` / meta the package already emits.

## PHP

```php
SEOService::setData(new SEOData(title: 'Home', description: '...'));
echo SEOService::render();

// Tests / non-Blade:
resolve(TagManager::class)->for(new SEOData(...))->render();
```

No data set → only `<title>{site_name}</title>` + `noindex, nofollow, noarchive`. Intentional; do not invent titles.

## Recipes

```php
// Minimal
new SEOData(title: 'Contact', description: 'Get in touch');

// Draft
new SEOData(title: $draft->title, noindex: true);

// Article + hreflang + schema
new SEOData(
    title: $post->title,
    openGraphTitle: $post->socialTitle,
    description: $post->excerpt,
    image: $post->coverPath,
    type: 'article',
    publishedAt: $post->published_at,
    modifiedAt: $post->updated_at,
    section: $post->category?->name,
    tags: $post->tags->pluck('name')->all(),
    canonicalUrl: $post->canonical_url,
    lang: $post->hreflangUrls,
    schema: [Schema::fAQPage()->mainEntity(/* ... */)],
);
```
